                <pb facs="0454" n="382" sameAs="frus:frus1909/pg382"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 6775/628.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Secretary of the First Central American
                            Conference.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1909-01-21"><hi rendition="#italic">January 21,
                        1909</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I receive with much pleasure your telegram announcing the results reached by the
                    First Central American Conference during the sessions which closed to-day. This
                    evidence of the agreement of the representatives of the five Republics on
                    measures of mutual benefit and common advantage is of happy augury for harmony
                    and good will in Central America.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Elihu Root.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
